Similarly, if we plug in $x = -a$ and $y = b,$ then
\[|x + y| + |x - y| = |-a + b| + |-a - b| = |a - b| + |a + b| \le 4.\]This means $(-a,b)$ is also a point in the region.  Therefore, the region is symmetric around the $y$-axis.

